  "name": "Tsymbaly folk orchestra (Belarusian State Folk Orchestra)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Orchestral folk music of Belarus led by the tsymbaly, the Belarusian trapezoidal hammered dulcimer, represented here by the generic hammered-dulcimer card, together with bayans and string bass, in the manner of the State Folk Orchestra of Belarus, the oldest musical collective in the country. The tsymbaly virtuoso Iosif Zhinovich, founder of the Belarusian professional tsymbaly school, was among its founding musicians and later led it as artistic director and conductor; the orchestra now bears his name, and its recordings were issued by Melodiya.",
